{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5","id":1529664,"title":"How to use Pentex in W5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-29T13:29:36-08:00","id":1529664,"title":"How to use Pentex in W5?","content":"Pretty much what the title says.<br /> <br /> How do you figure Pentex should be used and what changes from previous editions, if any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T15:29:54-08:00","id":1529669,"title":"","content":"Same way it was used in the previous editions as a little known force hidden behind multiple layers of local shell companies and minor subsidiaries.....though from my reading of W5 even major subsidiaries are completely mundane companies with completely mundane resources so there's not much to do about them AS Garou and they are better opposed via human proxies or Garou who have lost the wolf so the can work alongside human NGOs and Class Actions.<br /> <br /> Though there are still references to First Teams it's not entirely clear at what point or how they would be deployed with no one ' in the know' to make the call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T18:14:37-08:00","id":1529678,"title":"","content":"I can't comment on the use of PENTEX in W5, but I definitely have opinions on how PENTEX should be used as I've change it extensively in my chronicles. Too often, the presentation of PENTEX is along these lines:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kh1CqCAc2fE\" data-code=\"Kh1CqCAc2fE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Kh1CqCAc2fE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I find that unsatisfying.<br /> <br /> I've basically divided PENTEX into three separate groups. The first is a Deep Umbral conspiracy to anti-terraform the planet. The second are those companies somehow engaged in supernatural evil. And the third are more mundane companies that can be used as placeholders for real world ills or parodies.<br /> <br /> &quot;PENTEX&quot; itself is a worldwide supernatural conspiracy of Deep Umbral entities seeking to kill Gaia and replace the world-soul with another. It is basically They Live as defined by this quote (I looked for an actual video of it on YouTube, but couldn't find it.):<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cLook at the world environment we live in. Carbon dioxide, fluorocarbons, and methane have increased since 1958. Earth is being acclimatized. They are turning our atmosphere into their atmosphere.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It's a combination of They Live, War of the Worlds, Videodrome, and Stargate.<br /> <br /> The Deep Umbral entities arrived post-WWII after open air nuclear weapon testing disrupted Earth's magnetic field enough to allow the first Deep Umbral invaders to bypass Gaias natural defenses. Their intention is to anti-terraform Earth into an entirely new ecosystem so that those \u201cspirits\u201d can arrive and make this planet their new home. After arriving, they presented themselves as as patrons of mankind, always helping them advance to the next stage of evolution. They claim to be responsible for uplifting mankind and steering the earliest human civilizations. They now claim to want to help humanity enter \u201cthe next age of man\u201d - genetic changes to prolong life and improve their ability to survive the great Earth Changes that are coming (becoming fomori). These entities were able to make limited contact with humans prior to the nuclear age, but it was very limited. They are mostly a post-1945 phenomenon (and they suffered a major defeat when international treaties banned future open air nuclear tests as it now prevents arrival of new Deep Umbral spirits to Earth).<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThey made contact with various people in industrialized countries in order to pollute the world. They unleash industrial pollutants, toxins, and greenhouse gases not because they seek to destroy our world, but to make it more like their own home. Likewise, they want to seize control of caerns and corrupt them so they'll serve their purposes and accelerate these processes. The humans they recruit can eventually become the &quot;Toad&quot; fomori. When they made contact with people in the Free World, they presented themselves as democratic. When they made contact with people in the Communist World, they presented themselves as socialist. After the Cold War, they would present themselves as technocratic internationalists or whatever. They change their story as needed for their intended audience. They provide new technology (some of which isn't technological, but explicitly Wyrm fetishes and the like that are simply so &quot;advanced&quot; as to seem like magic) to their new friends and allow them to increase their personal power and wealth.<br /> \u200b<br /> The Toads are spread all throughout the world in politics, business, media, etc. Some Toads do completely control some companies, industrial plants, or scientific institutions, but many are only partially corrupted. They do control various &quot;security&quot; firms and the like to strike at the Garou and their allies (aka &quot;terrorists&quot; like the Green Knights) when needed, but are more likely to manipulate things to prevent violence from happening at all. They also have access to processes that create guardians (animal fomori) or strange, terrifying creatures not from this world. Garou call it PENTEX because they've noticed a motif of the number five occurring among these creatures (it is a sacred number to them for some reason).<br /> <br /> So if the PENTEX evil is basically just pollution, this is what I go with. It's about 90% of what most people think of as PENTEX. I can name drop a lot of the same fictional subsidiaries or even use real companies or similar roman-a-clefs.<br /> <br /> The next group are subsidiaries that I've linked to a very specific supernatural evil which likely has nothing to do with pollution. My version of Endron drills for oil not because of greenhouse gas emissions, but because there is something trapped within the Earth that they are releasing. My version of Black Dog Game Factory is explicitly being controlled by Banes whose purpose is to entice people to give away their souls to evil creatures and spirits. My version of Avalon toys is controlled by supernatural entities wanting to exploit children and ruin innocence it's about haunted dolls, corrupting magic kits, play goo with strange transformative properties and the like. My version of Magadon is about humans uncovering ancient &quot;alchemy&quot; and other pseudo-science that transformed people into fomori and thus &quot;curing&quot; them of whatever horrible disease they had. My version of Tellus is controlled by a corrupted Weaver Automata that manifests as an AI behind Tellus Games like the MCP in Tron. It's threat is limited to computing, the internet, and its magical spinoffs like the Digital Web and the Cyberrealm. \u200bThese all have explicit supernatural threats. Most of them have no connection to the PENTEX conspiracy, but some like Endron do have certain interests in common and may cooperate.<br /> <br /> The last group are companies I name drop because they are known, but aren't actually involved in anything supernatural. O'Tolley's is just another shitty chain restaurant because I haven't thought of a good hook for them. Same with a lot of other single paragraph subsidiaries like Consolidex, King Breweries, or Circinnius Brands. I just don't see much opportunity for supernatural evil in consumer brands. They might do a lot of mundane harm, but they are generally not controlled by supernatural evil. Though individual offices and the like might be manipulated by lone agents like vampires, BSDs, certain fomori, etc. This level of &quot;evil&quot; can be fought by kinfolk activists and the like. In so far that Garou get involved, it's not combat against monsters. But there is always opportunity for more subtle powers and actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T19:49:55-08:00","id":1529685,"title":"","content":"Fantastic stuff, @Black Fox<br /> <br /> I admit, I'm currently thinking of the idea of Pentex being the dog that has caught the car. They've successfully transformed not only their own companies into engines of spiritual corruption and capitalism but they have managed to change the nature of capitalism itself.<br /> <br /> Basically, all of the corporations are copying Pentex's methods now.<br /> <br /> It's just the way business is done now.<br /> <br /> And those evil-evil ways are resulting in plenty of spiritual corruption and Bane's aiding/possessing people by themselves.<br /> <br /> So Pentex is LOSING ground to competitors and can't offer anything more to their masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T06:10:25-08:00","id":1529704,"title":"","content":"My take is that Pentex creates a more toxic environment on a personal and a global level simply because it\u2019s an ongoing car crash between shameless mega corporation, at least one greedy occult conspiracy and several varieties of raw Supernatural Evil: it is, in a nutshell, a horrible mess in the same way that a hydra is an ongoing tangle of heads that can still wreck terrible damage.<br /> <br /> Heck, if it were better organised at the top it might actually be <i>easier</i> for the Garou to deal with this particular monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, while Pentex is too big to fall in a single battle, it\u2019s not too big to fail - it\u2019s the Megacorporation other Megacorporations love to hate (creating the possibility of turning villains against a real monster), it\u2019s quite horribly inefficient (So there\u2019s a very real chance Our Heroes can do serious damage and get out before the left hand realises it\u2019s missing a partner) and the Corporation is no more immune to reflexive conservatism, backbiting &amp; culture wars than the Garou Nation (Arguably being much <i>more</i> at risk, since most of the Garou Nation are fighting for their Planet and their People, while most of Pentex just wants to make money).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an evil leviathan, but it\u2019s not invincible: the problem is that it\u2019s enemies have to be clever and <i>patient.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T04:32:36-08:00","id":1531460,"title":"","content":"I am currently compiling data to create something like &quot;Pentex subsidiaries strategy guide&quot; and post it on Storyteller's Vault. I have to admit that I was &quot;raised&quot; on previous editions but I will try to make it useful for W5 too. But, If I have to advice you, find something legal but morally dubious and exploit it to the limit. Remember 2 things: primo, Pentex is not just a corporation, it's a version of apocalyptic cult so they don't have to make profit, they just have to survive long enough to rule the world after the apocalypse (or, in worst case, they want to burn with it but for now it's imposible cause not only garou fight them but also most of the humanity). But still, they have to raise salaries of their low level employees but not of brainwashed upper management. They can even use it to win some people's hearts showing that they care for people. And secundo they are ahead of their competition because of their &quot;free labor force&quot; in Scar. So an example of using it: surely you noticed that if you buy bigger bottles of soda or food you pay less for a liter or kilo. And what if it's oposite at Herrick's? The smaller packages will be cheaper? They don't even have to make fomori, they will just drown us in thrash. Is it legal? Basically yes. OK, they propably will be an investigation if they don't set prices below the cost of production but I doubt that the investigation will reach Umbra. Is it morally dubious? Only if you see the long time effect. Is it effective? Yes it is.<br /> <br /> In my games Pentex is almost unbeatable because basically it doesn't do anything evil (at least not directly most of the time). They just want humanity to buy their products. And they have a way to &quot;enforce&quot; it by adding bonuses for being a loyal Pentex subsidiaries customer (basically it's legal and they can be really really big):<br /> <br /> Simon A. Mann goes shopping to Herrick's after his shift at DFG. There he buys Avalon doll for his daughter, Tellus FPS and Sunburst phone for his son and Vesuvius Publishing book for his other daughter. Then he buys King beer and Circinus cigarettes for himself, Pangloss lipstick for his wife. He knows that those are safe, Aesop Research Company tested them. To feed his family he buys some tuna from Hallahan fishing and Young&amp;Smith INC. bread and butter. He also buys new Rainbow tires for his car. He's a happy man, the discount is so big and he didn't even need to carry a big photo album with coupons. He's of course a proecological man: he packs his stuff to Good House paper bag and takes it to his electrically propelled Falcon Pathfinder. Kids are hungry so the happy family goes to O'Tooleys. Then he goes to the Endron Oil gas station. It's the tornado season so he needs some fuel for his emergency generator. He pays less because his salary comes to the Consolidex Worldwide bank account. After that they all visit his father, a legless Desert Storm veteran (his Nastrum fighter was shot down over Baghdad) in Autumn Health Management System nursing home. His father gets the care for free because Simon is a Vesuvius newspapers subscriber. They will also visit his other son. He is currently at Homogenic. He's gay and this is inexcusable sin for a true patriot's son (and Simon is a patriot, he fought for his country, so does his father and grandfather and of course he buys american). It's certainly that Spooky Tooth heavy metal band's fault. Maybe this new RPG from Black Dog will help him. Yes, he has four children, thanks to Conceptual Services. Then he goes home, build in the suburbs of Jackson, MS by High Quality Builders. He could afford it because there was Omni TV subscription bundle and thanks to the company he works for his electricity bill from Atlas is much lower. There he meets his buddy from the Army, Joseph Grant. They fought together during Iraqi Freedom. Joe is a gunsmith and he repaired Simon's old hunting rifle made by Herculean. He needs it cause there was some bear/Big Foot sightings nearby. He also notices that Ardus Waste Management took his trash finally. After a little workout with Dr. Veridan workout program (as any Serpent Brother and Tau Upsilon Phi member would do) and a dose of Magadon vitamine supplement he sits on a couch. &quot;This will be a good evening&quot; he thinks. First there will be a new episode of &quot;Concrete Dreams&quot; (Omni TV exclusive), then Friday Fight Night, pay per view Extreme Wrestling Warfare show, after that NASCAR (&quot;this new Endron Sponsored driver, car #77, Samuel Ross is the embodiement of American Dream; hope he won't kill himself on the track like those two last guys who forgot that this car is so fast&quot;) and then &quot;Slayer XIV&quot;, new Slaughterhouse horror. And if he won't fall asleep he could also watch Pigeon River Howlers concert on RED TV (he always liked bluegrass). &quot;Tomorrow I have to remember to send this month charity checks to Save Our Schools society and The Fellowship, they do so much good for every children in the States&quot;. Yup, this was a good day. And yes, Simon and his family could smell like Malfeas and still could be a normal, mortal family. Could you kill Simon, his wife Annie and his kids: Grace, Faith and little Johnny, Biff (Big Intimidating F*****g Fenrir)?<br /> <br /> So IMHO the only ways to topple Pentex is to buy them (highly unlikely, but in one of the Time of Judgement scenario they were bought of by Weaver), catch them on something illegal or morally wrong (the first is difficult to survive the second is a challenge for roleplaying a Press conference to show that to masses and even then it can end by sacrificing some middle management for &quot;Stepping out of line&quot;; just like in Robocop 2) and an attack on Scar en masse (it could be most effective as it would cripple their production capabilities but none of my players didn't try it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 02-25-2024, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T04:48:45-08:00","id":1531465,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, there won't be any more Werewolf subsidiaries for the time being but will be modules. And the next module will be Pentex focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:46:22-08:00","id":1531520,"title":"","content":"Really, when you get down to it PENTEX is an umbrella under which one can smuggle in some Black Comedy to make Monkey-wrenching (and generally being a Garou) less of a glum uphill struggle.<br /> <br /> Also, in a game line built in making a considerable part of Modern Society The Enemy, it never hurts to have a layer of deniability between you and the lawsuit brigade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:47:04-08:00","id":1531521,"title":"","content":"Gah, that was silly of me - since lawyers are sharks, logically Lawsuits should come in \u2018squadrons\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:13:39-08:00","id":1531550,"title":"","content":"As far as the official W5 presentation goes, the upcoming supplement &quot;Scent of Decay&quot; will be interesting.<br /> <br /> Here's the blurb for the supplement:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rotting from the inside.</b><br /> <br /> Milton has become a company town, and that company is Pentex. Between the rent-a-cops, the wasp fomori and the malicious spirits life there gets harder every day. Can a single pack of Garou scrape off the rot and turn Milton into territory they actually want to hold?<br /> <br /> Scent of Decay presents guidance for character creation and three pre-written stories set in the same small town and scenes which can be included in any Werewolf chronicle:<br /> <br /> <b>The Break Room:</b> A corporate fulfillment center seeks productivity at a terrible human cost<br /> <b>Shadows on the Prison Walls:</b> A trickster spirit tries to use the Garou for their own ends<br /> <b>A Pound of Flesh:</b> A rival pack and their patron spirit challenge Milton\u2019s Garou </div> </div> </div>But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> mentioned Justin Achilli's position had been that the subsidiaries of previous editions wouldn't be part of W5. Will the Renegade-writers still follow that same route... who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:57:18-08:00","id":1531554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531521#post1531521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Gah, that was silly of me - since lawyers are sharks, logically Lawsuits should come in \u2018squadrons\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slews, around here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where did all these Rokea come from and why do they <i>all</i> have four or five dots in Law, with a specialty in lawsuits?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T06:13:01-08:00","id":1531615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531550#post1531550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> mentioned Justin Achilli's position had been that the subsidiaries of previous editions wouldn't be part of W5. Will the Renegade-writers still follow that same route... who knows...</div> </div> </div> </div>For now IMHO it looks like they can't decide if they want W5 to be something new or to be a continuation. On one hand they try to create something new on the other they use parts of the previous editions in corebook (like quotes from signature characters or descriptions of example caerns). For now I try to make homebrew rules for W5 to be a continuation or rather to make it a pararell universe for W20 (I currently run a campaign which would propably end during ToJ and my PCs moves will decide what shape the world will take). The same could be for Pentex.<br /> <br /> On one hand the old version is quite qood. Big corporations united in one goal. They cover most of the products the modern world needs. So how they could replace it? By changing names? They could also try different approach, by dividing Pentex more, to the point of being small manufactures. Imagine many Pentexes concentrated in different states or countries. It would suit more for the W5 garou as more territorial than in W20.<br /> <br /> And if you add a third hand (fomori's maybe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) there was Pentex (yes, not one of the subsidiaries) commercial in one cutscene of an unreleased Heart of Gaia video game. It would put Pentex on plain sight. It would make life easier for Pentex as they won't need to hide connections between subsidiaries. Even if it would put Board of Directors in the light they could have hidden bosses (and we basically would have something like a secret cult from Call of Cthulhu). Or, after death of one of them, they shares could be bought by an another investor who would replace the fallen one.<br /> <br /> Either way if Pentex structure remains the idea of using legal but morally dubious ways still stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T07:03:58-08:00","id":1531618,"title":"","content":"I am a simple man. I have the view that if you have a license for a game world and market it as part of said license, it should be a continuation rather than a reboot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T08:02:49-08:00","id":1531621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531618#post1531618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a simple man. I have the view that if you have a license for a game world and market it as part of said license, it should be a continuation rather than a reboot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. Even if they try to make it one with V5 (which is a continuation) explaining the changes would be easier than anyone think. Especially with some parts of V5 setting specifically point to Werewolf's older editions (like Anita Wainwright searching for werewolves who slayed her friends during War in Chicago).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T13:54:25-08:00","id":1531645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531615#post1531615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For now IMHO it looks like they can't decide if they want W5 to be something new or to be a continuation. On one hand they try to create something new on the other they use parts of the previous editions in corebook (like quotes from signature characters or descriptions of example caerns). For now I try to make homebrew rules for W5 to be a continuation or rather to make it a pararell universe for W20 (I currently run a campaign which would propably end during ToJ and my PCs moves will decide what shape the world will take). The same could be for Pentex.<br /> <br /> On one hand the old version is quite qood. Big corporations united in one goal. They cover most of the products the modern world needs. So how they could replace it? By changing names? They could also try different approach, by dividing Pentex more, to the point of being small manufactures. Imagine many Pentexes concentrated in different states or countries. It would suit more for the W5 garou as more territorial than in W20.<br /> <br /> And if you add a third hand (fomori's maybe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) there was Pentex (yes, not one of the subsidiaries) commercial in one cutscene of an unreleased Heart of Gaia video game. It would put Pentex on plain sight. It would make life easier for Pentex as they won't need to hide connections between subsidiaries. Even if it would put Board of Directors in the light they could have hidden bosses (and we basically would have something like a secret cult from Call of Cthulhu). Or, after death of one of them, they shares could be bought by an another investor who would replace the fallen one.<br /> <br /> Either way if Pentex structure remains the idea of using legal but morally dubious ways still stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see how this all shakes out when we get our hands on the upcoming W5 supplement. I mean with that blurb of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; at the beginning of the W5 corebook, this could go in all sorts of directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T14:09:07-08:00","id":1531650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531645#post1531645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We'll see how this all shakes out when we get our hands on the upcoming W5 supplement. I mean with that blurb of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; at the beginning of the W5 corebook, this could go in all sorts of directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But as nobody said that V5 and W5 are separate settings (and as I said before a few things in V5 show that they aren't) I would rather see more detailed past of werewolves in W5 than a new version of Pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T17:08:27-08:00","id":1531656,"title":"","content":"According to the author of the two released adventures he hasn't actually established anything.....despite establishing things like Sept Positions, the name of the CoF originator Tribe and CoF using Clockwork Orangesque torture as a conversion tool.....so I'm not really sure what to make of that. Though I was told twice ' this is not W20' despite my questions actually being about and directly highlighting things that varied from the W5 corebook and not mentioning W20 at all.......so I'm not really sure whats up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T19:01:10-08:00","id":1531662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531656#post1531656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the author of the two released adventures he hasn't actually established anything.....despite establishing things like Sept Positions, the name of the CoF originator Tribe and CoF using Clockwork Orangesque torture as a conversion tool.....so I'm not really sure what to make of that. Though I was told twice ' this is not W20' despite my questions actually being about and directly highlighting things that varied from the W5 corebook and not mentioning W20 at all.......so I'm not really sure whats up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems very much like Ubisoft denying that The Division series is political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T00:07:07-08:00","id":1531667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531656#post1531656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the author of the two released adventures</div> </div> </div> </div>You said two. I know &quot;The deepest of wounds&quot; but what about &quot;Reclamation&quot;? I tried to find it but I couldn't. Do you know where I can get it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T02:28:52-08:00","id":1531670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531656#post1531656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the author of the two released adventures he hasn't actually established anything.....despite establishing things like Sept Positions, the name of the CoF originator Tribe and CoF using Clockwork Orangesque torture as a conversion tool.....so I'm not really sure what to make of that. Though I was told twice ' this is not W20' despite my questions actually being about and directly highlighting things that varied from the W5 corebook and not mentioning W20 at all.......so I'm not really sure whats up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way this could make sense to me is if the approach for W5 is now that W5 is intentionally vague and broad in its lore/worldbuilding and there are no official answers as such. So, for example, there's no official W5 answer to the question of how a Sept works and what Sept Positions there are. And so whenever a writer mentions details about those sorts of things, that stuff isn't any more &quot;true&quot; than whatever you could come up with as an ST at your table with your players.<br /> <br /> But does this mean that they're okay with individual writers contradicting each other in these supplements because it's just up to whatever these writers want to do (because they aren't interested in keeping the lore/worldbuilding coherent between different writers)? And if W5 is stepping back like that, why wouldn't it be fine for the official message to be &quot;And if you want to use old lore from W20 and previous editions to describe things like Septs and Sept-positions, you can.&quot; instead of emphasizing &quot;And please be aware that this is not a continuation of W20 and previous editions.&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531667#post1531667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said two. I know &quot;The deepest of wounds&quot; but what about &quot;Reclamation&quot;? I tried to find it but I couldn't. Do you know where I can get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Renegade-program where you register with them that you're doing a public gaming-event (be it online, at a gaming-store and/or a convention) and after Renegade have made sure you're legit, they send you the pdfs for these introductory one-shots to the games Renegade offers. Reclamation is the W5-one in that collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T08:50:34-08:00","id":1531686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529664-how-to-use-pentex-in-w5?p=1531670#post1531670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Renegade-program where you register with them that you're doing a public gaming-event (be it online, at a gaming-store and/or a convention) and after Renegade have made sure you're legit, they send you the pdfs for these introductory one-shots to the games Renegade offers. Reclamation is the W5-one in that collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thanks. So it's out of my reach. I don't run games for anyone but my group and I don't see any reason to change it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T10:45:44-08:00","id":1531689,"title":"","content":"Pentex I think is pretty much the model-Antagonist, but in a way I believe every gaming table should just pick a conglomerate company or other imperialistic entity they despise and use the model over it. I mean, I would even tell the authors to call the shovel a shovel, but we all know making big billionaire companies angry isn't a smart business tactic, and will get you a pretty harsh law suit. <br /> <br /> But we the players can do so in our own games.<br /> <br /> The Garou hit-list should be as simple as ordering a Forbes magazine or looking up top richest companies. That is true Pentex for ya. Any real-life big corporation will have the same elements as Pentex, if not even more terrible.<br /> <br /> But if you want a more conspiratory, big network, master behind the puppets, kind of game, then yeah, Pentex is great. Starting small, with small business closing, people on the street, crime rising, misery setting in, spirits starting to reflex that, and all things lead to the big franchise store opening, and after dealing with it (with all the ethic-crunching of beating poor workers who just want to pay rent), you see that it goes deeper, they operate on a model, and every city or neighborhood has the same store. So you got to go to the source, and it actually turns into a Lord of the Rings, James Bond/Jason Bourne/John Wick deal, or even something like Memento. Hell, you could go reverse Cybernet, you could be the Terminator who comes from down all the way to bite the big central computer's ass.<br /> <br /> The thing is, for me, Pentex is just too big, even if you are going against a Subsidiary, it comes to a point where no matter how cool your pack is, it needs backup. Werewolf is a game about finding out that even if you are big bad scary wolf, with a pack of them, you can't take on them alone, you need the Tribe, you need the Nation. So a big heist or reverse Helm's Deep scenario need to take place, organize many packs to take down the source of Wyrm//Weaver corrupted flow (so that they may be brought back to balance, city by city, region by region).<br /> In the end, fighting the spirits and security forces here and there is easy, but when you really need to take down the infrastructure, the HQ, the head, that dominates the region, you NEED the help of the other packs. Cuz Pentex is its own Nation, and every Subsidiary is it's own Tribe, working optimally alongside one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:16:14-08:00","id":1531960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-